<title>GERMANY: Spar plans to take over 36 Kathreiner supermarkets.</title>
<headline>Spar plans to take over 36 Kathreiner supermarkets.</headline>
<dateline>SCHENEFELD, Germany 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>German retail group Spar AG said on Wednesday that it plans to take over 36 supermarkets from the Kathreiner AG group with a turnover of 220 million marks ($131.7 million), net of VAT.</p>
<p>The supermarkets have sales areas of between 400 square metres and 2,000 square metres and are mostly situation in the states of Bavaria and Saxony, Spar said in a compulsory statement.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.671 German Marks)</p>
